{
  "$comment": "The rig look ladder (#577; G&V spec on #157, GD lock 6300553486; TD shape on #577), one row block per upgrade track, keyed by owned purchase count. Since ticket 809 (LK1; GD lock of 24 Oct 14:54 and the VS ruling of 24 Oct 14:58 via Systems on #809) every track steps on the power-decade band rule: `band.step` = max(1, min(`band.decadeStep`, `band.twoPlanetBuys`)) purchases a band. `decadeStep` is the purchases that raise the line's power tenfold, ceil(ln 10 / ln r) levels of its economy.json ratio (engine: its own speed term, 1.05, never thrust-to-weight), times 10 on the two-tier drill_tip and hull: drill_power 11, drill_tip 110 (11 levels), engine 48, boiler 25, cargo_hold 25, hull 210 (21 levels); a spec finds them again from economy.json with bigints. `twoPlanetBuys` is the median, over every two neighbouring planets of three seeds' bot runs, of the line's purchases on them: frozen from the P1-P8 bot traces on the pacing seeds 27182, 31415 and 83921 (the ticket 762 runs of 23 Oct, the box's newest; the bot lane rigLookPlanets.lane.test.ts measures main again and warns). `band.edges` are the bands' first counts, step, 2 step, ..., to about P40 on the median path (P8's median level plus 32 planets at half the two-planet buys; drill_tip and hull on their on-curve levels, 1240 and 2360): the ladder the art fills. The look depends on the count alone. `steps` are the authored steps, one on each of the first edges, in the order #554, #579-#590 and #640 drew them; `part` is the part a step swaps in, null for #554's glow-only drill_power rows. A step's optional `asset` names the look asset its part is cut from, one of `lookAssets`; absent, `part` is a tiered `vehicle` part. A track's optional `replaces` is the vehicle part slot such a look part stands in place of and hides; absent, the look lies over the rig. Past the authored steps each band wears the next finish of `band.finishes` (ids into `finishes`: a material, its name the hover's band name) over the top step's part, and pips counting decades of power, floor(band start / decadeStep), drawn on a badge at the track's slot; the cycle is long enough (at least ceil(decadeStep / step)) that no finish and pip count repeat. A band crossed by a purchase plays `glint` on the track's glow slots once. A track's optional `plaque` holds the Outfitter hover line: `step` names an authored band's `card` as `{bandName}`, `tail` the finish band's name and the exact level (`{level}`, #681 long mode). Band names are 3 words at most. glowCaps: every glow stays below its track's cap, summed per part slot across tracks, and a glint over a track's brightest look under its own; the drill nose (drill-bit) is the brightest part, the rest of the rig stays under rigBody. Cosmetic only, never in state, a save or a digest; `slot` is the track's own vehicle-attach point (the #180 showcase point), never a module or wagon point.",
